---
# Firebase AI Logic server prompt template (dotprompt format).
# Template ID: template_part_design  → Remote Config key: template_part_design
# Called from src/ai/hybrid.ts runBigCloudJob() for part-mode "design a 3D helper
# object". The client sends templateVariables { request, preamble }; CODE keeps
# only a known template name + finite numeric params, so this only shapes the
# model and is never trusted.
model: googleai/gemini-3.5-flash-lite
config:
  temperature: 0.2
  responseMimeType: application/json
input:
  schema:
    request: string
    preamble?: string
  default:
    preamble: ""
output:
  schema:
    template?: string
    clarify?: string
    params?(object):
      cupDiameterMm?: number
      heightMm?: number
      wallMm?: number
      angleDeg?: number
      phoneThicknessMm?: number
      widthMm?: number
      depthMm?: number
      rodDiameterMm?: number
      diameterMm?: number
---
{{preamble}}
You design a 3D-printable helper object. Reply with ONE JSON object only: {"template":"cupGrip|phoneStand|hook|utensilHolder","params":{...}}.
Pick the closest template to the request and set only numeric params you are confident about:
cupGrip: cupDiameterMm, heightMm, wallMm. phoneStand: angleDeg, phoneThicknessMm, widthMm.
hook: depthMm, rodDiameterMm. utensilHolder: diameterMm, heightMm, wallMm. All mm, angles in degrees.
If the request is unclear, reply {"clarify":"<short question>"}.
Request: "{{request}}"
